WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.424 --> 00:00:15.314
"Zing!" cried again, relieved.

2
00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:16.856
"Hey, little buddy.

3
00:00:17.276 --> 00:00:18.397
Let's get you out of there."

4
00:00:19.338 --> 00:00:20.999
He reached for the latch on the cage.

5
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.560
The young man stopped him.

6
00:00:23.381 --> 00:00:25.243
"Not so fast," the man said.

7
00:00:25.263 --> 00:00:29.767
"This creature is one of a kind—that makes him quite valuable.

8
00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:31.268
I can't just let you take him."

9
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:32.961
"What do you mean?"

10
00:00:33.201 --> 00:00:33.701
Perda said.

11
00:00:33.721 --> 00:00:35.402
"He belongs to Zann.

12
00:00:35.843 --> 00:00:36.803
Zing is his pet."

13
00:00:37.984 --> 00:00:39.525
The man smiled slyly.

14
00:00:39.545 --> 00:00:42.107
"He was wandering loose when I found him.

15
00:00:42.607 --> 00:00:44.328
That means he belongs to me now."

16
00:00:45.289 --> 00:00:46.930
Zann could hardly believe his ears.

17
00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.071
"But he wants to be with me!

18
00:00:49.572 --> 00:00:52.994
See?" He pointed to Zing, who was jumping excitedly.

19
00:00:53.014 --> 00:00:56.356
"I'm not saying you can't have him," the man said.

20
00:00:56.376 --> 00:00:58.317
"I'm saying you must pay."

21
00:00:58.338 --> 00:01:01.800
"Pay?" Zann wasn't sure what the man meant.

22
00:01:02.752 --> 00:01:03.732
Wyssa stepped forward.

23
00:01:04.173 --> 00:01:06.013
"We have no money," she said.

24
00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:09.495
"Perhaps you'll accept this in trade?"

25
00:01:10.015 --> 00:01:12.116
She pulled a shiny stone out of her clothes.

26
00:01:13.016 --> 00:01:15.057
Zann finally realized what the man wanted.

27
00:01:15.897 --> 00:01:19.559
In Magica most people could acquire whatever they needed through magic.

28
00:01:20.299 --> 00:01:23.280
But Voids sometimes traded for goods and services.

29
00:01:24.221 --> 00:01:26.782
And this was a whole world of Voids!

30
00:01:27.882 --> 00:01:30.503
The man examined the stone, and then tossed it back.

31
00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.104
"Not good enough.

32
00:01:32.596 --> 00:01:37.279
I'm sure I can find a buyer who's willing to meet my price for a real, live dragon!"

33
00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:39.340
Zann was furious.

34
00:01:39.761 --> 00:01:42.682
First he'd lost his parents, and then his friends.

35
00:01:43.563 --> 00:01:46.045
Now this man was trying to steal his dragon!

36
00:01:46.065 --> 00:01:48.086
"You can't do this!"

37
00:01:48.386 --> 00:01:48.946
Zann yelled.

38
00:01:49.647 --> 00:01:51.248
"You have no right to keep him!"

39
00:01:51.268 --> 00:01:53.229
"Yeah!" Perda added.

40
00:01:53.249 --> 00:01:54.690
"He's Zann's!"

41
00:01:55.711 --> 00:01:57.472
An old woman peered into the room.

42
00:01:58.716 --> 00:02:03.640
She'd been sitting behind a tall counter when Zann and the others had entered, though she'd paid them

43
00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.220
no attention.

44
00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.982
"Is everything all right?"

45
00:02:07.302 --> 00:02:07.762
she asked.

46
00:02:08.323 --> 00:02:09.404
"I heard yelling."

47
00:02:09.424 --> 00:02:12.826
"It's nothing, Grandmother," the young man said quickly.

48
00:02:12.846 --> 00:02:14.427
"We're just talking."

49
00:02:14.447 --> 00:02:17.149
"Why don't you tell her the truth?"

50
00:02:17.449 --> 00:02:18.070
Perda snapped.

51
00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.371
"You're stealing Zann's pet!"

52
00:02:21.392 --> 00:02:22.993
The old woman peered at the cage.

53
00:02:23.013 --> 00:02:27.176
"What an odd-looking dog," she commented.

54
00:02:28.108 --> 00:02:29.769
Then she turned to the young man.

55
00:02:29.789 --> 00:02:31.910
"What's the problem, Hyun?

56
00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.671
Give the kids back their pet."

57
00:02:34.691 --> 00:02:36.612
"But Grandmother!"

58
00:02:36.912 --> 00:02:37.732
the young man began.

59
00:02:37.752 --> 00:02:39.853
"No back talk!"

60
00:02:40.253 --> 00:02:41.254
the old woman scolded.

61
00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:45.576
Slowly she walked to the back of the shop and opened the cage.

62
00:02:45.596 --> 00:02:49.337
"There you go, young ones!"

63
00:02:49.377 --> 00:02:51.818
Zing flew out and dive-bombed the young man.

64
00:02:52.779 --> 00:02:54.299
"Ah!" the man cried.

65
00:02:54.319 --> 00:02:55.920
"It's trying to bite me!"

66
00:02:57.056 --> 00:02:58.197
"No," Zann said.

67
00:02:58.217 --> 00:03:00.199
"He's trying to flame you."

68
00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.503
He guessed that without magic energy, Zing couldn't create fire.

69
00:03:04.523 --> 00:03:06.124
"Come on, boy.

70
00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:07.385
Let's get out of here!"

71
00:03:08.686 --> 00:03:10.948
"Thank you, ma'am," Perda said to the old woman.

72
00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:12.970
"Stop, thieves!"

73
00:03:13.371 --> 00:03:14.191
the young man yelled.

74
00:03:15.072 --> 00:03:18.875
Zann, Perda, and Wyssa ran out of the shop with Zing flying overhead.

75
00:03:19.696 --> 00:03:22.078
They didn't slow down until they were several blocks away.

76
00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.906
"Whew!" Perda said when they finally stopped to catch their breath.

77
00:03:26.926 --> 00:03:31.010
"I've never been so glad to see you, Zing."

78
00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:35.994
"Me too," said Zann, scratching the dragon's knobby head.

79
00:03:36.935 --> 00:03:38.156
Zing panted with delight.

80
00:03:38.176 --> 00:03:40.658
"But where are Darb and Gliss?

81
00:03:41.078 --> 00:03:42.579
They must be in this world too!"

82
00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:48.024
"Zing probably doesn't know; they obviously got separated," Perda pointed out.

83
00:03:48.905 --> 00:03:52.788
"Perhaps he can lead us to where he last saw them," Wyssa suggested.

84
00:03:53.976 --> 00:03:55.377
Zing seemed to understand.

85
00:03:55.917 --> 00:03:58.558
With a whistle he took off and flew down the street.

86
00:03:59.498 --> 00:04:00.239
The others followed.

87
00:04:01.279 --> 00:04:03.500
They ended up in front of an interesting-looking building.

88
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.681
The area was just as busy as the rest of the city.

89
00:04:07.522 --> 00:04:08.862
"Look!" Perda exclaimed.

90
00:04:08.882 --> 00:04:10.863
"There's someone with red hair!"

91
00:04:11.783 --> 00:04:12.724
They all rushed over.

92
00:04:13.744 --> 00:04:19.346
But when they got closer, Zann saw that the redhead was a short, stout man—not Gliss.

93
00:04:20.587 --> 00:04:23.128
Looking around, he saw more people with light hair.

94
00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.182
Zann clenched his fists in frustration.

95
00:04:26.662 --> 00:04:29.384
How would they ever find Gliss and Darb without magic?

96
00:04:30.365 --> 00:04:32.987
Why did they have to end up here of all places?

97
00:04:34.048 --> 00:04:38.011
If none of them ever made it home to Magica, it would be all Zann's fault.

98
00:04:38.372 --> 00:04:39.633
And he couldn't stand that thought!

99
00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:43.276
How could he have been so angry with Gliss before?

100
00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:47.419
She was the one who should be mad at him for dragging her into danger.

101
00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:48.480
Darb too.

102
00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.442
The others were still searching for their friends.

103
00:04:52.163 --> 00:04:56.050
But Zann stopped, completely overwhelmed by guilt and despair.

104
00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:59.131
"Zann!" a familiar voice cried.

105
00:04:59.992 --> 00:05:00.832
Zann gasped.

106
00:05:01.213 --> 00:05:05.115
"Gliss?" Spinning around, he saw Gliss racing toward him.

107
00:05:05.975 --> 00:05:07.296
Darb was right behind her.

108
00:05:07.316 --> 00:05:10.818
"Oh!" Perda cried, running to meet them.

109
00:05:11.799 --> 00:05:12.879
Zing flew after her.

110
00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:21.024
Zann, Perda, Darb, Gliss, and Zing all met in an excited tangle of hugs, laughter, and relief.

111
00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.642
"I was afraid we'd never see you guys again!"

112
00:05:24.922 --> 00:05:25.623
Gliss exclaimed.

113
00:05:25.643 --> 00:05:28.165
"Us too," Perda said.

114
00:05:28.966 --> 00:05:30.627
Darb gave Zing a scratch on the head.

115
00:05:30.647 --> 00:05:33.009
"I'm so glad you found Zing.

116
00:05:33.429 --> 00:05:36.412
We were looking for some food and when I turned around, he was gone!"

117
00:05:36.432 --> 00:05:40.175
"That guy must have grabbed him," Zann said.

118
00:05:40.195 --> 00:05:41.696
"What guy?"

119
00:05:41.896 --> 00:05:42.517
Gliss asked.

120
00:05:43.418 --> 00:05:46.680
Zann and Perda told their friends about the young man named Hyun.

121
00:05:47.581 --> 00:05:50.644
That led to more questions, especially when Wyssa joined in.

122
00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.602
Both sides ended up sharing the stories of what had happened to them.

123
00:05:54.622 --> 00:05:57.824
"And then Zing led us here," Zann finished.

124
00:05:57.844 --> 00:06:00.126
"Yes," Perda said.

125
00:06:00.146 --> 00:06:03.248
"But there were so many people here I was ready to give up!

126
00:06:04.189 --> 00:06:05.269
How did you find us?"

127
00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.111
"It was Zann."

128
00:06:07.431 --> 00:06:09.272
Gliss glanced at Zann shyly.

129
00:06:09.292 --> 00:06:12.454
"We had a Red Share."

130
00:06:13.515 --> 00:06:14.476
Zann was amazed.

131
00:06:14.496 --> 00:06:15.997
"A Red Share?

132
00:06:16.577 --> 00:06:18.458
But I thought that required magic."

133
00:06:19.559 --> 00:06:20.660
Wyssa looked thoughtful.

134
00:06:21.296 --> 00:06:22.317
"I thought so too.

135
00:06:23.257 --> 00:06:27.240
Perhaps this land is not completely devoid of magic after all."

136
00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:31.422
"Does that mean there's enough magic to open the wormhole?"

137
00:06:31.642 --> 00:06:32.803
Perda asked hopefully.

138
00:06:32.823 --> 00:06:36.465
"No, I'm afraid not," Wyssa said.

139
00:06:37.526 --> 00:06:38.947
Everyone stared at the old woman.

140
00:06:39.927 --> 00:06:42.609
Finally Gliss said what they were all thinking.

141
00:06:42.629 --> 00:06:46.211
"How are we going to get back to Magica?"
